.SH NAME
ssoossh-service - Get certificates for unattended jobs, from an enrollment code.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh service [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Certificates for unattended jobs. A person runs \fBservice enroll\fR once and approves it in the browser, which produces an enrollment code. The job then runs \fBservice retrieve\fR with that code, with no browser, for as long as the enrollment lasts.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for service


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to an extra config file, merged after the standard locations

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address, e.g. https://ssh.example.com; https is assumed when no scheme is given

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


